@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il29-time`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-individual`
IMPORT `ito-il29-test-people`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-29 tests: s 1 "Israeli resident" (a), the Regulations of 5766-2006 and s 14(b).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew text BEFORE the code was run; the arithmetic is in the
-- comment beside it.  A failing assertion is a finding: none has been edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`resident` i `under` r MEANS `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a): an Israeli resident in the tax year of` i `under` r

`D` MEANS `the default readings of row IL-29`

§ `The day-count presumptions, (a)(2)`

-- (a): 183 days or more in the tax year.  183 -> presumed in Israel; 182 (and nothing else) -> no presumption.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 183 `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 182 `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
-- 365 days in 2026 (not a leap year) is allowed; 366 is more than the days in the year.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 365 `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 366 `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the days in Israel given are negative or exceed the number of days in the tax year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` (0 MINUS 1) `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the days in Israel given are negative or exceed the number of days in the tax year"
-- 2028 is a leap year: 366 days allowed.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2028 `, days` 366 `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D`

-- (b): 30 days or more in the tax year and 425 or more in the tax year and the two before it.
-- 30 + 200 + 195 = 425 -> presumed.   30 + 200 + 194 = 424 -> not.   29 + 365 + 365 = 759 but 29 < 30 -> not.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 30 `,` 200 `,` 195) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 30 `,` 200 `,` 194) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2026 `, days` 29 `,` 365 `,` 365) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
-- the presumption alone, without the layers around it
#ASSERT `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on` 30 `days in the tax year,` 200 `in the tax year before it and` 195 `in the one before that`
#ASSERT NOT `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on` 30 `days in the tax year,` 200 `in the tax year before it and` 194 `in the one before that`
#ASSERT NOT `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on` 29 `days in the tax year,` 365 `in the tax year before it and` 365 `in the one before that`
#ASSERT `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on` 183 `days in the tax year,` 0 `in the tax year before it and` 0 `in the one before that`
#ASSERT NOT `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on` 182 `days in the tax year,` 242 `in the tax year before it and` 0 `in the one before that`

§ `The finding of the centre of life, (a)(1) and (3)`

-- A finding governs whatever the days: outside Israel with 200 days; in Israel with 10.
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `, days` 200 `,` 200 `,` 200 `, whose centre of life was found` `outside Israel`) `under` `D`
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `, days` 10 `,` 0 `,` 0 `, whose centre of life was found` `in Israel`) `under` `D`

§ `A rebutted presumption, (a)(3), fork C2`

-- 200 days, rebutted, no finding: the text says the presumption can be rebutted (by either) and does not say a
-- rebuttal places the centre of life outside Israel.  Default declines; the other reading says not resident.
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `, days` 200 `,` 0 `,` 0 `, whose presumption was rebutted`) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the presumption was rebutted and no finding says where the centre of life then is: the text does not say that a rebuttal itself places the centre of life outside Israel"
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `, days` 200 `,` 0 `,` 0 `, whose presumption was rebutted`) `under` (`the defaults, except rebuttal read` `a rebutted presumption finds the centre of life outside Israel`)
-- A "rebuttal" where no presumption arose is not a rebuttal of anything: the ordinary decline.
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `, days` 100 `,` 0 `,` 0 `, whose presumption was rebutted`) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"

§ `The ties, (a)(1), fork C1`

-- 100 days, no finding: five ties all in Israel.  The text lists the ties as factors in a weighing of the whole
-- ("מכלול"), so the default declines; the other reading takes unanimous ties as the finding.
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with` 100 `days and the ties` (`ties that all lie` `lies in Israel`)) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with` 100 `days and the ties` (`ties that all lie` `lies in Israel`)) `under` (`the defaults, except ties read` `ties that all lie one way find the centre of life there`)
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with` 100 `days and the ties` (`ties that all lie` `lies outside Israel`)) `under` (`the defaults, except ties read` `ties that all lie one way find the centre of life there`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with` 100 `days and the ties` `ties that lie both ways`) `under` (`the defaults, except ties read` `ties that all lie one way find the centre of life there`) BECAUSE "the ties named do not all lie one way, so even on the reading that unanimous ties find the centre of life they do not find it"
-- A presumption that is not rebutted stands over ties that all point abroad (the ties are no finding).
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with` 183 `days and the ties` (`ties that all lie` `lies outside Israel`)) `under` (`the defaults, except ties read` `ties that all lie one way find the centre of life there`)

§ `Counting days from stays, (a)(2)`

-- 2026: 1 Jan - 30 Jun = 31 + 28 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 = 181 days; 1 Aug - 2 Aug = 2 days (arrival and departure
-- days count); total 183 -> presumed.  With 1 Aug - 1 Aug (a single day, part of a day is a day) -> 182.
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A stay in Israel`
`a stay from` a `to` b MEANS `A stay in Israel` WITH `arrived` IS a, `left` IS b

GIVEN y  IS A NUMBER
      ss IS A LIST OF `A stay in Israel`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`an individual in` y `with the stays` ss MEANS
    `the individual in` y `with` (`counted from the stays` WITH `the stays` IS ss) `, found` NOTHING `, ties` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE `, regulation 2` NOTHING `, regulation 3` NOTHING `, section 14(b)` NOTHING

#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30)), (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 8 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 2)))) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `with the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30)), (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 8 1) `to` (YMD 2026 8 1)))) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
#ASSERT `the days in Israel in` (`the calendar tax year` 2026) `, from the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30))) EQUALS 181
-- A stay across the year-end: 20 Dec 2025 - 10 Jan 2026: 12 days in 2025 (20..31) and 10 in 2026 (1..10).
#ASSERT `the days in Israel in` (`the calendar tax year` 2025) `, from the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2025 12 20) `to` (YMD 2026 1 10))) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the days in Israel in` (`the calendar tax year` 2026) `, from the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2025 12 20) `to` (YMD 2026 1 10))) EQUALS 10
-- A stay wholly outside the year counts nothing.
#ASSERT `the days in Israel in` (`the calendar tax year` 2026) `, from the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2025 3 1) `to` (YMD 2025 3 31))) EQUALS 0
-- Two stays that share a day (one ends 30 Jun, the next begins 30 Jun) would count 30 Jun twice.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the days in Israel in` (`the calendar tax year` 2026) `, from the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30)), (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 6 30) `to` (YMD 2026 7 5))) BECAUSE "two of the stays share a day, so the days would be counted twice: give one stay for the days they cover"
-- A stay that ends before it begins.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the days in Israel in` (`the calendar tax year` 2026) `, from the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 6 30) `to` (YMD 2026 6 1))) BECAUSE "a stay in Israel ends before it begins"

-- Three tax years from the stays: 2024: 1 Jul - 31 Dec = 31+31+30+31+30+31 = 184; 2025: 1 Jan - 30 Jul = 181 + 30 = 211
-- (31+28+31+30+31+30 = 181, plus July 1..30 = 30 -> 211); 2026: 1 Mar - 30 Mar = 30.  Sum 184 + 211 + 30 = 425 -> presumed.
-- 2025 stay to 29 Jul -> 210 -> 424 -> not.   2026 stay to 29 Mar -> 29 days (< 30) -> not, whatever the sum.
GIVEN j IS A NUMBER
      k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`an individual who was in Israel from 1 July 2024, to 30 July 2025 less` j `days, and in March 2026 for` k `days` MEANS
    `an individual in` 2026 `with the stays` (LIST (`a stay from` (YMD 2024 7 1) `to` (YMD 2024 12 31)),
                                                   (`a stay from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `to` (Date (Day (YMD 2025 7 30) MINUS j))),
                                                   (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (Date (Day (YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS (k MINUS 1)))))

#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual who was in Israel from 1 July 2024, to 30 July 2025 less` 0 `days, and in March 2026 for` 30 `days`) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual who was in Israel from 1 July 2024, to 30 July 2025 less` 1 `days, and in March 2026 for` 30 `days`) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual who was in Israel from 1 July 2024, to 30 July 2025 less` 0 `days, and in March 2026 for` 29 `days`) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"

§ `The tax year, s 1 "שנת מס"`

-- "תקופה של שנים עשר חדשים רצופים, שתחילתה ב־1 בינואר": 365 days in 2026 and 366 in the leap year 2028.
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the calendar tax year` 2026) EQUALS 365
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`the calendar tax year` 2028) EQUALS 366
-- "ואם נקבעה תקופת שומה מיוחדת – תקופת השומה שנקבעה כאמור": a special assessment period from 1 Jan to 30 Jun 2026 is 181 days.
`a half-year special assessment period` MEANS `a tax year that is the special assessment period` 2026 `from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `to` (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` `a half-year special assessment period` EQUALS 181
-- The days in Israel in that tax year cannot exceed its 181 days; 181 days in a tax year of 181 days is not 183, so no presumption.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`a plain individual in the special assessment period, days` a MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH
        `the tax year`                 IS `a half-year special assessment period`
        `the tax year before it`       IS `the calendar tax year` 2025
        `the tax year before that`     IS `the calendar tax year` 2024
        `the days in Israel`           IS `days counted` a `,` 0 `,` 0
        `the centre of life, as found` IS NOTHING
        `the ties`                     IS NOTHING
        `the presumption has been rebutted, by the individual or by the assessing officer` IS FALSE
        `employment facts for regulation 2` IS NOTHING
        `facts for regulation 3`       IS NOTHING
        `facts for section 14(b)`      IS NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in the special assessment period, days` 182) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the days in Israel given are negative or exceed the number of days in the tax year"
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in the special assessment period, days` 181) `under` `D` BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"

§ `The tax years this row answers`

-- Before 2024 the text of the provisions is not held (assumption A1, as row IL-08).
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2023 `, days` 365 `,` 365 `,` 365) `under` `D` BECAUSE "row IL-29 does not hold the text of these provisions for a tax year before 2024"
#ASSERT `resident` (`a plain individual in` 2024 `, days` 366 `,` 0 `,` 0) `under` `D`

§ `Section 14(b): the adjustment year`

-- A first-time resident arrives on 1 Mar 2026.  The adjustment year runs 1 Mar 2026 - 28 Feb 2027 (one year from
-- the day of arrival; the Nth anniversary itself is outside, assumption A3).  His centre of life is found in Israel.
GIVEN notice IS A MAYBE DATE
      y      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` notice `, in the tax year` y MEANS
    `the individual in` y `with` (`days counted` 300 `,` 0 `,` 0) `, found` (JUST `in Israel`) `, ties` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE `, regulation 2` NOTHING `, regulation 3` NOTHING
        `, section 14(b)` (JUST (`Facts for the adjustment year of section 14(b)` WITH
                                   `a first-time resident or a veteran returning resident` IS TRUE,
                                   `the day he arrived in Israel` IS YMD 2026 3 1,
                                   `the day he gave notice of the election` IS notice))

-- Window readings for the tax year 2026 (1 Jan - 31 Dec 2026) against the window 1 Mar 2026 - 28 Feb 2027:
--   whole tax year in the window: 1 Jan 2026 is before 1 Mar -> no;  some day: yes;  last day (31 Dec 2026): yes;
--   the first tax years counted from 2026 (N = 1): 2026 >= 2026 and 2026 < 2027 -> yes.
-- Tax year 2027 (1 Jan - 31 Dec 2027): whole no; some day yes (1 Jan 2027 <= 28 Feb 2027); last day (31 Dec 2027) no;
--   count: 2027 < 2027 -> no.
-- Notice on 15 Apr 2026 is 45 days after arrival: in time on either reading of the 90 days.
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window`)
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the last day of the tax year lies in the window`)
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the tax year is among the first tax years counted from the tax year of the start`)
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the whole tax year lies in the window`)
-- The default declines: the readings give "not regarded as resident" and "resident".
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` `D` BECAUSE "section 14(b) may or may not displace the definition in this tax year: the text does not say how the 90 days run or how the adjustment year is matched with a tax year that it overlaps"
-- 2027 under the last-day reading: the adjustment year is over by 31 Dec 2027, so he is resident on his finding.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2027) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the last day of the tax year lies in the window`)
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2027) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window`)
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2027) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the tax year is among the first tax years counted from the tax year of the start`)
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2027) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the whole tax year lies in the window`)
-- 2028 is outside the window on every reading: all readings agree, so the default answers (resident).
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)) `, in the tax year` 2028) `under` `D`

-- The 90 days.  Notice on 30 May 2026: 1 Mar -> 31 Mar = 30 days, -> 30 Apr = 60, -> 30 May = 90 days after arrival.
--   day of arrival not counted: the 90th day after it is in time (90 <= 90);   day of arrival counted as the first: 90 > 89, late.
-- With the window read "some day", the tax year 2026 is in the adjustment year, so:
--   in time -> not regarded as an Israeli resident;   late -> the election failed, so resident on his finding.
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 30)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window` `and ninety days read` `the day of arrival is not counted, so the 90th day after it is in time`)
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 30)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window` `and ninety days read` `the day of arrival is the first day, so the 90th day counting it is in time`)
-- Default 90 days, window "some day": notice on day 90 is in time on one reading and late on the other: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 30)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window`) BECAUSE "section 14(b) may or may not displace the definition in this tax year: the text does not say how the 90 days run or how the adjustment year is matched with a tax year that it overlaps"
-- Notice on 31 May is 91 days after: late on both readings, so no reading of the window matters and the default answers.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 31)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` `D`
-- Notice on 29 May is 89 days after: in time on both readings (89 <= 89), so the window decides; with "some day": not resident.
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 29)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window`)
-- No notice given: no election.
#ASSERT `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` NOTHING `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` `D`
-- A notice dated before the day of arrival: the text does not say that it is within 90 days of it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`a first-time resident who arrived on 1 March 2026 and gave notice` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)) `, in the tax year` 2026) `under` `D` BECAUSE "the notice of election is dated before the day of arrival, and the text does not say whether that is within 90 days of it"

§ `Regulations of 5766-2006 reg 2: individuals deemed Israeli residents`

-- His centre of life is found outside Israel, so the definition alone says he is not resident; reg 2 may deem him one.
GIVEN y  IS A NUMBER
      em IS AN `An employer named in paragraph (4) of the definition`
      began IS A BOOLEAN
      abroad IS A MAYBE DATE
      proved IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`an individual in` y `found outside Israel, employed by` em `, began while resident:` began `, began abroad on` abroad `, proved otherwise:` proved MEANS
    `the individual in` y `with` (`days counted` 20 `,` 20 `,` 20) `, found` (JUST `outside Israel`) `, ties` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE
        `, regulation 2` (JUST (`Employment facts for regulation 2` WITH
                                   `the employer` IS em,
                                   `the individual works for that employer in the tax year` IS TRUE,
                                   `the employment relationship began while he was an Israeli resident` IS began,
                                   `the day he began to work for that employer outside Israel` IS abroad,
                                   `he proved to the assessing officer that he is not to be deemed a resident` IS proved))
        `, regulation 3` NOTHING `, section 14(b)` NOTHING

-- reg 2(1): an employee of the State of Israel, whose employment began while he was an Israeli resident.  No time limit.
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `the State of Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` NOTHING `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2040 `found outside Israel, employed by` `the State of Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` NOTHING `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- reg 2(1) is not subject to the proof "אלא אם כן הוכיח אחרת", which closes (2) only (RES line 23).
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `the State of Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` NOTHING `, proved otherwise:` TRUE) `under` `D`
-- employment began when he was not resident: not deemed
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `the State of Israel` `, began while resident:` FALSE `, began abroad on` NOTHING `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- reg 2(2): a local authority; began working for it abroad on 1 Mar 2022: five years run to 28 Feb 2027.
--   2026 (1 Jan - 31 Dec 2026) is inside on every reading (whole yes; some yes; last yes; count: 2026 >= 2022 and < 2027) -> deemed.
--   2027: whole no (31 Dec 2027 > 28 Feb 2027); some yes; last no; count: 2027 < 2027 no -> readings differ -> declined.
--   2028: no day inside (1 Jan 2028 > 28 Feb 2027); count: 2028 < 2027 no -> all no -> not deemed.
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a local authority in Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2027 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a local authority in Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "regulation 2 may or may not deem him an Israeli resident in this tax year: the text does not say how the five years from the day he began to work outside Israel are matched with the tax year"
#ASSERT `resident` (`an individual in` 2027 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a local authority in Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `some day of the tax year lies in the window`)
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2027 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a local authority in Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` (`the defaults, except windows read` `the last day of the tax year lies in the window`)
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2028 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a local authority in Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- proved otherwise to the assessing officer's satisfaction (reg 2(2) only): not deemed
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a local authority in Israel` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` TRUE) `under` `D`
-- an employer not named in paragraph (4): not within the regulation
#ASSERT NOT `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `an employer not named in paragraph (4)` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` (JUST (YMD 2022 3 1)) `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D`
-- the day he began to work abroad is needed for reg 2(2)
#ASSERT REFUSED `resident` (`an individual in` 2026 `found outside Israel, employed by` `a government company` `, began while resident:` TRUE `, began abroad on` NOTHING `, proved otherwise:` FALSE) `under` `D` BECAUSE "regulation 2(2) turns on the day he began to work for that employer outside Israel, and it was not given"
-- A boundary of the five years: 5 years from 1 Mar 2022 end on 28 Feb 2027 (the anniversary 1 Mar 2027 is outside, assumption A3).
#ASSERT `the last day of the window of` 5 `years from` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28

§ `Regulations of 5766-2006 reg 3: individuals deemed foreign residents`

-- He has the days of a resident (200 in the tax year), so (a)(2)(a) presumes his centre of life is in Israel; reg 3 may
-- deem him a foreign resident, which the power in (a)(4) allows ("לא יראו אותם ככאלה").
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      days  IS A `Days in Israel`
      imm   IS A BOOLEAN
      five  IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      cl    IS A `A class in regulation 3`
      arr   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`an individual in` y `with` days `, new immigrant:` imm `, foreign resident in the five years before:` five `, class` cl `, arrived` arr MEANS
    `the individual in` y `with` days `, found` NOTHING `, ties` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE `, regulation 2` NOTHING
        `, regulation 3` (JUST (`Facts for regulation 3` WITH
                                   `a new immigrant within section 35(d)` IS imm,
                                   `a foreign resident in each of the five preceding tax years, oldest first` IS five,
                                   `the class` IS cl,
                                   `the day he arrived in Israel` IS arr))
        `, section 14(b)` NOTHING

`five years of foreign residence` MEANS LIST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`four of five years of foreign residence` MEANS LIST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a diplomat` MEANS `a diplomatic representative or consular official of a foreign state in regular service and official capacity, or a spouse or child living with one`
`the 200 days` MEANS `days counted` 200 `,` 0 `,` 0

