§ `Section 14(a): a veteran returning resident`

-- Ten consecutive years as a foreign resident at least: 10 is enough, 9 is not (for a return outside 2007 to 2009).
#ASSERT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2026, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 10)
#ASSERT NOT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2026, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 9)
-- For a return in the tax years 2007 to 2009 read five years: 5 is enough, 4 is not; 2006 and 2010 are outside that note.
#ASSERT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2007, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 5)
#ASSERT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2009, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 5)
#ASSERT NOT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2008, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 4)
#ASSERT NOT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2006, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 5)
#ASSERT NOT `s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` (`A return to Israel` WITH `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` IS 2010, `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` IS 9)
